<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/CGS-Unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "<p>The C.G.S. System of Units defined four units of measure as a basic set from which all otherC.G.S units are derived. These are: </p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>length: cm = centimetre; </li>\r\n<li>mass: g = gram;</li>\r\n<li> time: s = second; </li>\r\n<li> luminous intensity: cd = candela, originally new candle.</li>\r\n</ol>"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/CGS-Unit> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/citation> "https://www.unc.edu/~rowlett/units/cgsmks.html" .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/CGS-Unit> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/citation> "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centimetre%E2%80%93gram%E2%80%93second_system_of_units" .
