<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/generalization> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This property relates a quantity kind to its generalization. A quantity kind, PARENT, is a generalization of the quantity kind CHILD only if:\r\n\r\n1. PARENT and CHILD have the same dimensions in every system of quantities;\r\n2. Every unit that is a measure of quantities of kind CHILD is also a valid measure of quantities of kind PARENT."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/generalization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
