<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A unit of measure, or unit, is a particular quantity value that has been chosen as a scale for measuring other quantities the same kind (more generally of equivalent dimension). For example, the meter is a quantity of length that has been rigorously defined and standardized by the BIPM (International Board of Weights and Measures). Any measurement of the length can be expressed as a number multiplied by the unit meter. More formally, the value of a physical quantity Q with respect to a unit (U) is expressed as the scalar multiple of a real number (n) and U, as  \\\\(Q = nU\\\\)."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
