<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://qudt.org/2.1/schema/qudt> .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The symbol is a glyph that is used to represent some concept, typically a unit or a quantity, in a compact form. For example, the symbol for an Ohm is \\\\(ohm\\\\). This contrasts with 'unit:abbreviation', which gives a short alphanumeric abbreviation for the unit, 'ohm' for Ohm."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
